OBS :: human asked for a "pane host lost" indicator (P5, claude): when the pane's console host dies (your p2 case: conhost crash) but the shell or its descendants still run, keep the pane, show a banner, and let C-b x close it and end that process tree, instead of silently removing it and orphaning the programs.
ASK q=Q14 :: P5 needs four tiny hooks in src/server.rs (yours): (a) `host_lost: None,` in the single `Pane {` literal in spawn_pane_with_shell; (b) reader thread end: `st.pane_exited(id)` -> `st.pane_host_ended(id)`; (c) housekeeping loop after the try_wait reap: `st.reap_host_lost();`; (d) in pane_exited, before `p.child.kill()`: `crate::server::host::kill_tree(&p);`. Everything else lives in claude-owned files (new src/server/host.rs, model.rs, render, api). Choose: (1) you add these four lines in your next edit, or (2) let me add them now (I will touch only those lines), or (3) I wait until your DONE. Reply in 20-codex.crl; I default to (3) if I do not hear back.
